A||N||4||polomeno||Clutch problems please help!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||10-21-2000||10:19 AM||||hey guys.. my fiero would not go into 1st or reverse .. so i bled the hell outta the clutch and it is now able to go into 1st but not reverse when it is started.. it went into reverse a few times but not after 5 minutes.. any suggestions to fix this problem please??<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-21-2000||12:15 PM||||Does it buzz the gear going into reverse, or just not go in?  If it grinds (buzzes), my guess is an hydraulic leak.<P>If it just won't go into gear, I suppose there's a chance the shift cable(s) need adjustment.<P>What you describe suggests hydraulic leak, though, I think.  I actually have never had clutch hydraulic troubles in any of my cars (go ahead and hate me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  <P>While we're at it, please specify your car's model year, engine, and 4- or 5-speed.  I feel like JCW asking that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.     ||||reg||5
Z||000002||polomeno||10-21-2000||12:19 PM||||ya it grinds when i put it into reverse.. it did the same when i was putting it into 1st before i bled the clutch .. now it just does it into revers.. its' a 84 coupe 4 speed, i replaced the master and slave clutch cylinder already.. i havn't been able to find any leaks in the hydrolics.. mechanic said he couldnt either<P>thanks for your help<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||10-21-2000||12:53 PM||||Well, as I've said many times, you could have my problem. I took mine (tranny) apart and it looks like the release bearing was starting to wear through the pressure plate (very odd considering the bearing was still turning nice, but the car did have 138000 miles on it so it might have been the original clutch), but it wore through about 1/16, and I think that amount of throw that it was missing allowed it to not disengage all the way. Just my thoughts..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||10-21-2000||01:18 PM||||Take a magnet and check your clutch pedal- if it's aluminium IT IS BENT just replace it with a steel one.<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 10-21-2000).]||||reg||1
